From 6b3ce4eda67b5ecdaaec459b2b939123ff9c2ac4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 04:10:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][PlayerInfo] A 3D Dolby Vision video says what went
 out and why, and Atmos says who renders its heights

The player information of a 3D Dolby Vision film (profile 20, side by
side) said three things that did not agree: "Output of this video" read
"Native Dolby Vision" (the label of the choice "as the settings say"
wherever the display takes native output), while the same page said
"SDR, not Dolby Vision" and "Rebuilt, mapped to SDR", with the reason
"not available for this video". Native output carries one picture and
never goes out in 3D: each view is rebuilt.

- The video stream of the video that plays is known to be 3D
  (DVBRIDGE::StreamIs3D(), from its stereo mode as it opens; "mono" is
  2D).
- "Output of this video" names its value "As the settings say (no
  native Dolby Vision in 3D)" for such a video on a display that takes
  native output, and offers no choice of native Dolby Vision for it
  (measured, its own over its HDR10+, made from HDR10+ or HLG), nor, for
  an HDR10, HDR10+ or HLG 3D video, "as Kodi plays it", which is what
  the settings give it then.
- The reason on the Dolby Vision page is "Dolby Vision is not sent in 3D:
  each view is rebuilt" (reason code stereo), unless Dolby Vision is
  turned off in the settings.
- The kodi.log line of such a stream no longer says that Dolby Vision is
  not used "natively or reconstructed" and that it plays from its base
  layer: it says that native output is not used, and that where Dolby
  Vision is rebuilt in 3D each view is rebuilt.

The badge of the sound named a passed-through Dolby Atmos stream of
E-AC-3 "DD+ Atmos 5.1": the 5.1 are the channels of its core, and the
heights are objects that the receiver renders. Passed through, an Atmos
stream now reads "DD+ Atmos 5.1 + objects" ("TrueHD Atmos 7.1.2 +
objects"); decoded here, where FFmpeg decodes the core alone and the
objects are left out, it reads "DD+ 5.1, no Atmos", so that a
receiver of heights that shows none is explained. The bytes that go to
the receiver do not change.

Strings: core #62868 and Estuary #54926 and #54927, in English and in
the three Spanish translations of Estuary. The pages for other skins
(system/hades) are made again from Estuary's files.
